type: software
title: "Order-polynomial positivity for width-two posets with a chain of at most five elements"
authors:
  - family-names: Goyal
    given-names: Dev D.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-9132-744X"
date-released: 2026-10-31
version: "1.0.0"
url: "https://github.com/dvgyl/math-and-theory/tree/main/papers/mathematics/width-two-order-polynomial"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: "Fully autonomous agentic research. For every finite poset that is the union of two chains, one of them with at most five elements and the other arbitrary, |P|! times the order polynomial has nonnegative coefficients, a case of a conjecture of Ferroni, Morales and Panova; the linear coefficient is at least (a-1)!(b-1)!m/(a+b)!. The proof combines the descent-rook correspondence, a chamber reduction to polynomials in the gaps and exact square certificates. Lean checks the certificates for chains of size at most four. Dev D. Goyal is responsible for publication. No expert validation or peer review is claimed."
keywords:
  - "order polynomial"
  - "width-two posets"
  - "Ehrhart positivity"
  - "order polytope"
  - "sum of squares certificate"
  - "Lean"
  - "autonomous agentic research"
